(1) In the notification, the notifying party must state:
1. whether
a) investigation proceedings for an act punishable by the criminal courts or criminal court proceedings are being conducted against it, or
b) criminal court proceedings have been conducted against it in the past;
2. whether administrative penal proceedings or comparable proceedings under another legal system are being conducted against it in connection with a business or other professional activity, or have been concluded with final effect with a penalty or a reprimand in the last five years;
3. whether it is or was involved as a debtor in insolvency proceedings, composition proceedings or comparable proceedings, provided that the period during which the insolvency database may be inspected has not yet expired. This also applies where comparable circumstances arose abroad;
3a. whether enforcement proceedings are pending against it as a debtor or enforcement measures have been taken against it in the last year;
4. whether a supervisory authority to whose supervision it is or was subject has opened an investigation or taken a measure against it in the last ten years, and whether and how any such proceedings were concluded;
5. whether a registration, authorisation, licence, membership or entitlement to carry on a trade or other professional activity has been refused, withdrawn, prohibited or revoked in its case in the last ten years by an authority, a court, another self-governing body or a professional representative body, or whether corresponding proceedings are being conducted;
6. whether, in the last five years, it has been given notice or summarily dismissed as an employee, or removed as a fiduciary, member of a foundation board (section 14(1) of the PSG), trustee (section 2, point 6) or from a comparable position of trust;
7. whether, in connection with a business or other professional activity, in the last five years the notifying party
a) was a party to administrative proceedings or civil court proceedings, where the proceedings are capable, alone or together with other information, of casting doubt on the integrity of the notifying party, or
b) has had a disciplinary measure imposed on it, including disqualification as a member of a management body.

(2) Criminal proceedings that were discontinued on legal grounds or for lack of sufficient suspicion, or that ended in an acquittal, need not be stated under subsection (1), point 1(b). Nor need criminal proceedings that ended by withdrawal from prosecution be stated where five years have passed since the withdrawal from prosecution, or convictions that have been expunged.

(3) The notifying party must also declare whether its reliability, or the reliability of a person under section 8(1), point 3 or 7, as an acquirer of a qualifying holding in a credit institution, an insurance or reinsurance undertaking, an investment firm, an investment services undertaking, a payment institution or an electronic money institution has been assessed by a supervisory authority competent for their supervision. It must also declare whether a comparable assessment has been carried out by another authority. Official documents that also show the outcome of the assessment must be attached to the notification. Where the notifying party does not have such documents, it must state the reasons.

(4) Where the notifying party is a natural person, the information required under subsection (1) must also be provided in respect of each undertaking under section 10, point 2 and each person under section 8(1), point 7. Where the notifying party is not a natural person, the information required under subsection (1) must also be provided in respect of all undertakings controlled by the notifying party, all persons and companies able to exercise significant influence over the notifying party and each person under section 8(1), points 3 and 7. Where information to be transmitted under this subsection is not available to the notifying party, it must state the reasons.

(5) The information under subsection (1), point 1 must be evidenced by a criminal record certificate or comparable foreign proof. The information under subsection (1), points 2, 3 and 7 must be evidenced by certificates issued by authorities, where available.

