(1) In the deposit business under section 1(1), point 1 of the Bankwesengesetz (BWG), BGBl. Nr. 532/1993, as amended by the Federal Act BGBl. I Nr. 118/2016, and in the giro business under section 1(1), point 2 of the BWG, there is a low risk of money laundering or terrorist financing in respect of the escrow accounts referred to in subsection (2).

(2) By way of derogation from section 6(3) of the FM-GwG, credit institutions (section 2, point 1 of the FM-GwG) may, in respect of customers, in relation to
1. pooled escrow accounts of lawyers or notaries;
2. escrow accounts of lawyers or notaries for deceased estates;
3. escrow accounts of lawyers or notaries for guardianships;
4. insolvency escrow accounts of lawyers or notaries;
5. escrow accounts of authorised property managers for communities of owners of real property under section 20(6) of the Wohnungseigentumsgesetz 2002 (WEG 2002), BGBl. I Nr. 70/2002, as amended by the Federal Act BGBl. I Nr. 87/2015,
apply the simplified customer due diligence measures laid down in sections 2 and 3.

(3) Even when applying the simplified customer due diligence measures under this Regulation, credit institutions must monitor transactions and business relationships to an extent sufficient to enable the detection of unusual or suspicious transactions.

(4) Credit institutions must not assume a low risk of money laundering or terrorist financing for the escrow accounts referred to in subsection (2) where the information available to them suggests that the risk of money laundering or terrorist financing is not low. In that case, the simplified customer due diligence measures laid down in this Regulation must not be applied.

(5) The determination of a low risk of money laundering or terrorist financing, the applicability of the simplified customer due diligence measures laid down in sections 2 and 3 in respect of customers in relation to the escrow accounts referred to in subsection (2), and subsections (3) and (4) also apply to CRR credit institutions that provide the activities under points 1 and 4 of Annex I to Directive 2013/36/EU on access to the activity of credit institutions and the prudential supervision of credit institutions and investment firms, OJ L 176, 27.06.2013, p. 338, as corrected by OJ L 208, 02.08.2013, p. 73, as last amended by Directive 2014/59/EU, OJ L 173, 12.06.2014, p. 190, in Austria through a branch under section 9 of the BWG.

